# Dynamic Cross-Correlation Matrices

This directory contains dynamic cross-correlation matrix (DCCM) data calculated from the equilibrated molecular dynamics trajectories.

The matrices describe correlated residue motions for the systems included in the manuscript. CSV files can be opened with spreadsheet or data-analysis software.

## File Contents

- Rows and columns correspond to residues.
- Matrix values represent pairwise motion-correlation coefficients.
- Residue numbering follows the model numbering described in the main repository README. The manuscript uses residue labels based on the original crystal structure numbering.

See the corresponding CSV files for system identifiers and matrix labels.
